  All facts below verified by reading actual registry sources under `~/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/` and the worktree's `Cargo.lock`/`Cargo.toml` at `/Users/smaschek/dev/paigasus/paigasus-helikon/.worktrees/sma-623`. `setup-protoc` is currently wired into 8 CI call sites: `ci.yml` (6x), `integration.yml`, `release-plz.yml`, `msrv.yml`.

  ## 1. temporalio-protos 0.9.0

  Path: `temporalio-protos-0.9.0/Cargo.toml` (from `Cargo.toml.orig`):

  ```
  [features]
  default = []
  serde_serialize = []
  grpc-clients = ["tonic/channel"]
  vendored-protox = ["dep:protox", "prost-types/vendored-protox"]

  [dependencies]
  anyhow = "1.0"
  base64 = "0.23"
  derive_more = { workspace = true }
  http = "1"
  prost = { workspace = true }
  prost-types = { workspace = true }
  serde = { version = "1.0", features = ["derive"] }
  serde_json = { workspace = true }
  thiserror = { workspace = true }
  tonic = { workspace = true, default-features = false, features = ["codegen"] }
  tonic-prost = { workspace = true }
  pbjson = { workspace = true }

  [build-dependencies]
  prost = { workspace = true }
  tonic-prost-build = { workspace = true }
  pbjson-build = { workspace = true }
  protox = { version = "0.9.1", optional = true }
  ```

  Note: the published (normalized) `Cargo.toml` shows the runtime dep resolves as `[dependencies.prost-types] version = "0.7", package = "prost-wkt-types"` — i.e. the manifest key `prost-types` is workspace-inherited to actually mean the crate `prost-wkt-types`, not the official `prost-types` crate. This matters for Q2.

  `build.rs` (`temporalio-protos-0.9.0/build.rs`, 201 lines) — key parts:

  ```rust
  #[cfg(feature = "vendored-protox")]
  use prost::Message;
  use tonic_prost_build::Config;
  ...
  fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
      println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=./protos");
      let out = PathBuf::from(env::var("OUT_DIR").unwrap());
      let descriptor_file = out.join("descriptors.bin");
      println!("cargo:descriptor_path={}", descriptor_file.display());
      let protos = &[
          "./protos/local/temporal/sdk/core/core_interface.proto",
          "./protos/api_upstream/temporal/api/sdk/v1/workflow_metadata.proto",
          "./protos/api_upstream/temporal/api/workflowservice/v1/service.proto",
          "./protos/api_upstream/temporal/api/nexusservices/workerservice/v1/request_response.proto",
          "./protos/api_upstream/temporal/api/operatorservice/v1/service.proto",
          "./protos/api_upstream/temporal/api/errordetails/v1/message.proto",
          "./protos/api_cloud_upstream/temporal/api/cloud/cloudservice/v1/service.proto",
          "./protos/testsrv_upstream/temporal/api/testservice/v1/service.proto",
          "./protos/grpc/health/v1/health.proto",
          "./protos/google/rpc/status.proto",
      ];
      let includes = &[
          "./protos/api_upstream", "./protos/api_cloud_upstream", "./protos/local",
          "./protos/testsrv_upstream", "./protos/grpc", "./protos",
      ];
      let mut builder = tonic_prost_build::configure()
          .build_server(false)
          .build_client(env::var_os("CARGO_FEATURE_GRPC_CLIENTS").is_some())
          // ... many .type_attribute()/.field_attribute() calls for derive_more::From/Display and
          // conditional serde derives via ALWAYS_SERDE / SERDE_ATTR over SERDE_DERIVE_PREFIXES ...
          .skip_debug(["temporal.api.common.v1.Payload"]);

      #[cfg(feature = "vendored-protox")]
      {
          let descriptors = protox::compile(protos, includes)?;
          std::fs::write(&descriptor_file, descriptors.encode_to_vec())?;
          builder = builder.skip_protoc_run();
      }

      builder
          .file_descriptor_set_path(&descriptor_file)
          .compile_with_config({ let mut c = Config::new(); c.enable_type_names(); c }, protos, includes)?;

      let descriptors = std::fs::read(&descriptor_file)?;
      pbjson_build::Builder::new()
          .register_descriptors(&descriptors)?
          .build(&[".temporal.api.failure", ".temporal.api.common", ".temporal.api.enums"])?;
      Ok(())
  }
  ```

  **Without `vendored-protox`**: `tonic_prost_build::configure().compile_with_config(...)` runs, which internally calls `prost-build`, which shells out to a real `protoc` binary (found via `PROTOC` env var or `PATH`) to produce the `FileDescriptorSet`, then generates Rust code from it. **With `vendored-protox`**: `protox::compile(protos, includes)` (pure-Rust, in-process) produces the `FileDescriptorSet` directly, `builder.skip_protoc_run()` tells `tonic_prost_build`/`prost-build` not to invoke `protoc` at all, and the rest of the pipeline (codegen from the descriptor, pbjson serde build) is identical and needs no protoc either way.

  Proto roots/includes: only the vendored copies under `temporalio-protos-0.9.0/protos/{local,api_upstream,api_cloud_upstream,testsrv_upstream,grpc,google}`. Well-known types (`google/protobuf/{timestamp,duration,struct,wrappers,any,empty,descriptor}.proto`) are **vendored inside the crate** at `protos/api_upstream/google/protobuf/*.proto` — not pulled from protoc's bundled include dir. `google/rpc/status.proto` and `google/api/{http,annotations}.proto` are likewise vendored.

  No `--experimental_allow_proto3_optional` or other special protoc CLI flags are used (this path never shells to protoc's CLI directly — `prost-build`/`tonic-prost-build` handle that internally when not skipped). `cargo:rerun-if-changed=./protos` is emitted once for the whole `protos/` directory (not per-file). The crate's `README.md` states explicitly: "Enable the `vendored-protox` feature to compile the protobuf definitions with the pure-Rust `protox` implementation instead of requiring an installed `protoc` binary."

  ## 2. `prost-types/vendored-protox` — important nuance

  **This is NOT a feature on the real, official `prost-types` crate.** In the exact locked version (`prost-types 0.14.4`, confirmed in this worktree's `Cargo.lock`), the `[features]` table is only `arbitrary`, `default = ["std"]`, `std` — **no `vendored-protox` feature exists on real prost-types 0.14.4**.

  The feature line `"prost-types/vendored-protox"` in `temporalio-protos`'s manifest is a Cargo dependency-rename reference: `temporalio-protos` declares its dependency under the manifest key `prost-types` but with `package = "prost-wkt-types"`, version `"0.7"` (resolves to `prost-wkt-types 0.7.2` in this lock). So the feature actually targets **`prost-wkt-types`**, whose real `Cargo.toml` has:

  ```
  [features]
  default = ["std"]
  schemars = ["dep:schemars"]
  std = []
  utoipa = ["dep:utoipa"]
  vendored-protoc = ["protobuf-src"]
  vendored-protox = ["protox"]
  ```

  `prost-wkt-types-0.7.2` has its own `build.rs` (`build = "build.rs"` in its manifest) which compiles 5 of its own vendored `.proto` files (`pbtime`, `pbstruct`, `pbany`, `pbempty`, `pbmask`, under its own `proto/` dir) via `prost_build::Config` + `.compile_well_known_types()`. Relevant excerpt:

  ```rust
  fn build(dir: &Path, proto: &str) {
      ...
      let mut prost_build = prost_build::Config::new();
      #[cfg(feature = "vendored-protox")]
      {
          let file_descriptors = protox::compile([source.clone()], ["proto/".to_string()]).unwrap();
          std::fs::write(&descriptor_file, file_descriptors.encode_to_vec()).unwrap();
          prost_build.skip_protoc_run();
      }
      prost_build
          .compile_well_known_types()
          .type_attribute("google.protobuf.Empty", "...")
          .type_attribute("google.protobuf.FieldMask", "...")
          .file_descriptor_set_path(&descriptor_file)
          .out_dir(&out)
          .compile_protos(&[source], &["proto/".to_string()])
          .unwrap();
      ...
  }
  ```

  So enabling `temporalio-protos/vendored-protox` transitively enables `vendored-protox` on `prost-wkt-types` too (via the rename), and **both** protoc call sites (temporalio-protos's own build.rs, and prost-wkt-types's build.rs) switch to protox. Without the feature, both fall back to real `protoc` (prost-wkt-types's `build.rs` has no fallback to a bundled protoc unless its separate `vendored-protoc` feature — which pulls `protobuf-src`, a C++ source build of protoc — is used instead; that feature is not wired anywhere in this workspace).

  ## 3. Feature forwarding through temporalio-common / temporalio-client, and the rest of the family

  **Confirmed the feature IS currently NOT enabled anywhere in this workspace.** Root `Cargo.toml:141-158`:

  ```
  temporalio-sdk      = { version = "1.0", default-features = false }
  temporalio-client   = { version = "1.0", default-features = false, features = ["tls-aws-lc"] }
  temporalio-sdk-core = { version = "0.9", default-features = false, features = ["tls-aws-lc"] }
  temporalio-common   = { version = "1.0", default-features = false }
  temporalio-macros   = { version = "1.0", default-features = false }
  temporalio-workflow = { version = "1.0", default-features = false }
  ```

  No `vendored-protox` feature is passed anywhere, and `Cargo.lock`'s dependency block for `temporalio-protos` (lines ~6216-6237) does **not** list `protox` as a dependency at all — confirming `vendored-protox` has never been resolved/built in this lock. `protox` itself is **absent from the local Cargo registry cache entirely** (`~/.cargo/registry/cache` and `~/.cargo/registry/src` — no `protox-*` anywhere), consistent with it never having been pulled in.

  Forwarding chain, quoted from each crate's `[features]`:

  - `temporalio-client-1.0.0/Cargo.toml`: `vendored-protox = ["temporalio-common/vendored-protox"]`
  - `temporalio-common-1.0.0/Cargo.toml`: `vendored-protox = ["temporalio-protos/vendored-protox"]`
  - `temporalio-protos-0.9.0/Cargo.toml`: `vendored-protox = ["dep:protox", "prost-types/vendored-protox"]` (as above)

  **`temporalio-sdk-1.0.0` and `temporalio-sdk-core-0.9.0` do NOT have a `vendored-protox` feature at all** — I read their full `[features]` tables and it is absent from both (their forwarding is only for `envconfig`, `tls-aws-lc`/`tls-ring`, `otel`, `prometheus`, `dynamic-tls`, `experimental`). `temporalio-workflow-1.0.0` only has `experimental = []`. `temporalio-common-wasm-1.0.0` only forwards `grpc-clients` and `serde_serialize`, not `vendored-protox`. `temporalio-macros-1.0.0` has no `[features]` at all.

  Practical implication: to retire system `protoc`, the feature must be turned on via the workspace's **direct** deps on `temporalio-client` and/or `temporalio-common` (both of which the root `Cargo.toml` already declares directly) — not via `temporalio-sdk`/`temporalio-sdk-core`, which have no path to it. Since Cargo unifies features per resolved package instance workspace-wide, enabling it on either edge still flips the single shared `temporalio-protos` and `prost-wkt-types` instances for the whole graph (including what `temporalio-sdk`/`temporalio-sdk-core` consume).

  **Build.rs inventory across the whole temporalio family** (checked every extracted source dir): only 3 build.rs files exist in the entire family + its prost-wkt-types dependency:
  1. `temporalio-protos-0.9.0/build.rs` — invokes protoc (or protox with the feature). Described in Q1.
  2. `prost-wkt-types-0.7.2/build.rs` — invokes protoc (or protox with the feature). Described in Q2.
  3. `temporalio-common-1.0.0/build.rs` — does **not** invoke protoc/protox at all. It only reads the already-compiled `FileDescriptorSet` bytes published by temporalio-protos via `links = "temporalio_protos"` / `DEP_TEMPORALIO_PROTOS_DESCRIPTOR_PATH`, and generates pure Rust codegen (`PayloadVisitor` impls, payload-limits validator) from that descriptor with `prost::Message`/`prost_types::FileDescriptorSet` — no external compiler invocation.

  `temporalio-client-1.0.0`, `temporalio-common-wasm-1.0.0`, `temporalio-macros-1.0.0`, `temporalio-sdk-1.0.0`, `temporalio-sdk-core-0.9.0`, `temporalio-workflow-1.0.0` all have **no `build.rs` file** in their extracted source directories at all.

  ## 4. protox

  `protox` is **not present anywhere in the local registry cache** (`~/.cargo/registry/src/*` and `~/.cargo/registry/cache/*` both have zero `protox*` entries) — it has never been downloaded/built in this workspace. Reported from crates.io/GitHub instead (network-verified, not local cache):

  - Version range required: `temporalio-protos` and `prost-wkt-types` both pin `protox = "0.9.1"` (build-dep, optional). Newest published version on crates.io is also `0.9.1` (no newer release exists), so `0.9.1` would be selected.
  - `protox 0.9.1` deps (from crates.io dependencies API): `bytes ^1.6.0`, `prost ^0.14.0`, `prost-reflect ^0.16.0`, `protox-parse ^0.9.0`, `miette ^7.2.0`, `thiserror ^2.0.0`, optional `clap ^4.5.4` (feature `bin`); dev-only: `prost-build`, `insta`, `tempfile`, `serde_json`, `serde_yaml`, etc.
  - `protox-parse 0.9.0` deps: `logos ^0.15.0`, `miette ^7.2.0`, `prost-types ^0.14.0`, `thiserror ^2.0.0` (all non-optional/normal), plus dev-deps.
  - MSRV: crates.io's authoritative `rust_version` field for the published `0.9.1` version is **`1.74.0`**, matching the repo's own README ("minimum Rust version requirement of 1.74+"). Note: the `main` branch's un-released Cargo.toml on GitHub shows a bumped `rust-version = "1.80.0"` — that is post-0.9.1 and not what would actually be pulled.
  - License: `MIT OR Apache-2.0`.
  - TLS/crypto: **none found**. Walking the full dependency tree (bytes, prost, prost-reflect, protox-parse, logos, miette, thiserror, prost-types) — none of these pull `ring`, `rustls`, `openssl`, `native-tls`, or any network/TLS crate. This is a pure local parser/compiler with no networking.
  - protoc-parity documentation: **not found**. I checked protox's README.md and CHANGELOG.md (both at the `protox-v0.9.1` tag) and its docs.rs page; none contain an explicit statement of feature differences from real `protoc` (editions support, custom options completeness, source-info generation, etc.). The README only states it is "an implementation of the protobuf compiler in rust, intended for use as a library," with `prost-build`/`tonic-build` integration examples and `miette`-based error reporting. I did not find documented limitations — report this as undocumented/unverified rather than asserting specific gaps.

  ## 5. Other build.rs files in the full dependency graph (the critical question)

  Extracted the full `Cargo.lock` package list (698 packages total; 673 resolve to real registry crates, 25 are this workspace's own path crates plus one crate — `console-0.16.6` — absent from the local cache but unrelated to protobuf). Of the 673 registry crates, **95 have a `build.rs`**. I grepped every one of those 95 for `protoc`, `prost_build`/`prost-build`, `tonic_build`/`tonic-build`, `compile_protos`, and `protox`, plus a separate pass for `Command::new("protoc"`, `which::which("protoc"`, and bare `PROTOC` env-var usage.

  **Result: only the 3 files already covered above matched** — `prost-wkt-types-0.7.2/build.rs`, `temporalio-common-1.0.0/build.rs` (false positive: its matches are just the substring "proto" inside comments/strings like "protocol Message body", not an actual protoc invocation — already confirmed above it does no compiler invocation), and `temporalio-protos-0.9.0/build.rs`. No other crate in the entire 673-crate resolved graph (all features) invokes protoc or a protoc-wrapping build tool.

  Specifically checked and ruled out by name:
  - `opentelemetry-proto-0.32.0` is in the lock but has **no `build.rs` at all** — it ships pre-generated/committed Rust code, no compile-time codegen.
  - `aws-sdk-bedrockruntime`, `aws-sdk-sso`, `aws-sdk-ssooidc`, `aws-sdk-sts` (the only AWS SDK crates in this lock) — none has a `build.rs`.
  - `quinn-proto` — present but this is QUIC "proto" (protocol), unrelated to protobuf; no protoc dependency.
  - No `google-cloud-*`, `tonic-build`-consuming, or `lance` crates are present in this lock at all.

  **Conclusion for Q5: no other crate in this workspace's dependency graph needs a system `protoc` binary.** The entire `setup-protoc` CI requirement traces back exclusively to the temporalio family, specifically to `temporalio-protos` and (transitively, via the `prost-types`→`prost-wkt-types` rename) `prost-wkt-types`. If the workspace turns on `vendored-protox` on its direct `temporalio-client`/`temporalio-common` deps (the feature doesn't route through `temporalio-sdk`/`temporalio-sdk-core`, so those must not be relied on to carry it), both remaining protoc call sites switch to the pure-Rust `protox` compiler, and `setup-protoc` becomes removable from all 8 CI call sites (`ci.yml` x6, `integration.yml`, `release-plz.yml`, `msrv.yml`), subject to whatever risk assessment the ticket wants to do on `protox`'s undocumented protoc-parity (point 4) and its added dependency footprint.

  Not found / could not verify: an explicit protox-vs-protoc feature-parity statement (editions, custom options, source-info) in protox's own docs — I looked and it isn't documented there, so don't cite unverified parity claims.

</agent-message>

